      "headline": "Senior Software Engineer",
      "about": "Ever since my childhood, researching and developing along with creativity has been my passion. I still remember when I was in middle school, I made a Hoffman's Voltameter, a mechanical switch and a charger from scraps and got appreciation for that from my teachers and people around.\n\nThis passion for technology continued to develop and I obtained an Electronics and Communication engineering degree . In academics I get to know about programming languages, algorithms and the fascination which drove me into engineering got wings. I started solving real world problems with the help of some electronics devices and some lines of codes. This was the first time I made money by making a water level controller.\n\nSo, now as a professional, this passion remains with me. There's certainly yet more to learn, yet more problems to solve, and yet more to build. And for this I am very grateful.\n\nWhen I am not working on software projects, I use to play and learn musical instruments and I find a beautiful connection between music and software. Also I spread knowledge about computer & technology to the community and  help younger ones to learn programming.\n\nSkills/Interests: Dart, Flutter,React.JS,  Python, SQL, OpenCV, NodeJS, AWS (EC2), Git, GitHub, Mobile Technology, C++, Hybrid Development, Artificial Intelligence/ Machine Learning, TensorFlow, Linux, Augmented Reality/Virtual Reality, Internet  of Things.",
